What are Aerospace Robots?
Aerospace robots are highly specialized automated systems engineered to perform precision tasks across aircraft manufacturing, maintenance, repair, and overhaul (MRO) operations, as well as space exploration missions. These robotic systems encompass a broad range of technologies, including articulated robots, collaborative robots (cobots), autonomous aerial vehicles, inspection drones, and robotic arms deployed for assembly, welding, painting, drilling, and non-destructive testing (NDT) applications within the aerospace sector.

